1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,423
Last one: freeze, seal, and preventExtensions. It's a

2
00:00:03,523 --> 00:00:06,613
short answer question, and it's easy points once

3
00:00:06,713 --> 00:00:09,140
you have one small table in your head.

4
00:00:11,233 --> 00:00:14,428
For each method, there are four questions. Can you add

5
00:00:14,528 --> 00:00:18,333
new properties, delete them, modify their values, and read them?

6
00:00:18,433 --> 00:00:22,566
preventExtensions is the mildest. You can't add new properties, but

7
00:00:22,666 --> 00:00:25,725
you can still delete and modify the existing ones.

8
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:29,579
seal goes one step further. No adding and no deleting, so the

9
00:00:29,679 --> 00:00:33,332
set of keys is locked. But you can still change the values.

10
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:36,935
freeze is the strictest. No adding, no deleting,

11
00:00:37,035 --> 00:00:40,116
and no modifying. The object is read only.

12
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:43,266
Notice the pattern: each row down removes one more

13
00:00:43,366 --> 00:00:46,812
permission. Reading is always allowed. And you can check

14
00:00:46,912 --> 00:00:50,612
an object's state with isExtensible, isSealed, and isFrozen.

15
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:57,392
Here's the exam's example. We make a game object and seal it.

16
00:00:57,466 --> 00:01:00,966
Adding a year is not allowed, because sealing blocks adding.

17
00:01:01,066 --> 00:01:03,414
Deleting the name is not allowed either.

18
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:07,456
But changing players is fine. Sealed objects can still be modified.

19
00:01:07,533 --> 00:01:10,167
In a normal, sloppy-mode script, the blocked

20
00:01:10,267 --> 00:01:13,337
changes don't throw. They're just silently ignored.

21
00:01:13,733 --> 00:01:16,637
So the name survives, players is 4, and

22
00:01:16,737 --> 00:01:20,257
year is undefined. It's sealed, but not frozen.

23
00:01:23,333 --> 00:01:27,433
But in strict mode, the same blocked changes throw TypeErrors.

24
00:01:27,533 --> 00:01:29,689
Both the add and the delete throw.

25
00:01:30,066 --> 00:01:33,960
Exam trap. Class bodies and modules are always strict, so in

26
00:01:34,060 --> 00:01:38,486
code like that, a blocked change throws instead of silently failing.

27
00:01:41,566 --> 00:01:43,386
preventExtensions on a car.

28
00:01:43,466 --> 00:01:46,187
Adding color is ignored, but modifying miles

29
00:01:46,287 --> 00:01:48,430
and deleting make are both allowed.

30
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:52,708
So only miles 20 is left, and isExtensible is false.

31
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:59,492
Last important detail: freeze is shallow. This team is

32
00:01:59,592 --> 00:02:02,372
frozen, and it has a nested stats object.

33
00:02:02,466 --> 00:02:05,798
Changing the name is ignored, and so is the delete.

34
00:02:05,866 --> 00:02:09,306
But team dot stats still points to the same inner object,

35
00:02:09,406 --> 00:02:12,846
and that object was never frozen. So changing wins works.

36
00:02:13,233 --> 00:02:15,005
Terps, and 10.

37
00:02:16,100 --> 00:02:20,337
Exam trap. Object dot freeze does not freeze nested objects. If

38
00:02:20,437 --> 00:02:24,400
you need them locked too, freeze each inner object as well.

39
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:31,225
Practice question 1. The pen is frozen. For each line, is the

40
00:02:31,325 --> 00:02:35,176
change allowed? And what's printed? Pause the video and try it.

41
00:02:43,466 --> 00:02:47,838
None of the three changes are allowed, because frozen means no

42
00:02:47,938 --> 00:02:51,589
add, no delete, and no modify. So it prints blue, 2,

43
00:02:51,689 --> 00:02:56,422
undefined, and true, because a frozen object also counts as sealed.

44
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:05,639
Practice question 2. Which method gives exactly this behavior? Modify yes,

45
00:03:05,739 --> 00:03:08,968
delete yes, add no. Pause the video and try it.

46
00:03:17,266 --> 00:03:20,886
Object dot preventExtensions. It only blocks adding.

47
00:03:24,966 --> 00:03:30,215
Recap. preventExtensions blocks adding. seal blocks adding and deleting, but you can

48
00:03:30,315 --> 00:03:35,055
still modify. freeze blocks all three, and it's shallow. Blocked changes are

49
00:03:35,155 --> 00:03:39,512
silently ignored in sloppy mode, and throw a TypeError in strict mode.

50
00:03:39,612 --> 00:03:42,314
That's the whole set. Good luck on the exam!

